    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build (dcf-methods routing row 1/2: US fabless semiconductor + patent licensing operating company; cyclical, so mid-cycle margins and a 14x cyclical cap rather than a growth-tech 20x). First valuation of QCOM; no prior DCF. FY0 = FY2026E (fiscal year ended 2026-09-27, not yet reported): revenue = 9M actual $32,798M + Q4 guidance midpoint $10,100M ($9.7-10.5B). FY26E reported FCF ~$9.3B = 9M OCF $8,405M - capex $1,578M + Q4 est ~$2.5B; owner FCF ~$4.85B (11.3% margin) after $4.45B SBC+withholding -- depressed by a weak Q3 OCF ($991M) and AI/data-center opex build; FY25 actual owner FCF was $8,922M (20.1%). Year-1 component-built owner FCF ~$6.6B (15.6%) sits between the two. Adj EBITDA here = GAAP operating income + D&A + SBC: FY22 44.5% (peak), FY23 33.7% (trough), FY24 37.0%, FY25 37.8%, FY26E ~32.7% (9M 33.8%, Q3 28.7%). Net debt from the Q3 FY26 balance sheet: total debt $15,270M (LTD $12,781M + current LTD $1,991M + CP $498M) less cash $4,533M and current marketable securities $3,771M. Interest income (~$450M/yr) NOT stripped: QCOM is net debt, and the engine builds unlevered flows from EBITDA, so neither interest income nor expense is in the projected FCF. QSI non-marketable venture stakes (~low $bn) are excluded from the bridge (conservative). Data center AI (AI200/AI250, HUMAIN 200MW, mgmt target $5B 2027 / $15B 2029) is NOT extrapolated at face value in base: base assumes it roughly offsets Apple modem attrition; only bull gives material incremental revenue.",
